{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "class NormalizedTuple:\n    @staticmethod\n    def normalize(a: int, b: int) -> tuple:\n        \"\"\"Normalizes a 2-element tuple to (min(a, b), max(a, b)).\"\"\"\n        return (min(a, b), max(a, b))\n\nclass OccurrenceCounter:\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the counter with an empty dictionary.\"\"\"\n        self.counts = {}\n\n    def count_tuples(self, list_of_2_element_tuples: list[tuple]) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Counts occurrences of normalized tuples in the given list.\"\"\"\n        for a, b in list_of_2_element_tuples:\n            normalized_key = NormalizedTuple.normalize(a, b)\n            self.counts[normalized_key] = self.counts.get(normalized_key, 0) + 1\n        return self.counts\n\ndef check_occurences(list_of_2_element_tuples: list[tuple]) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique 2-element tuples in a list after normalizing them to (min, max).\n    Returns a dictionary mapping each normalized tuple to its count.\n    \"\"\"\n    counter = OccurrenceCounter()\n    return counter.count_tuples(list_of_2_element_tuples)"}
